---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RelatedLinks from '../components/RelatedLinks.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../../site.config.mjs';
---
<BaseLayout title="Security">
  <p class="eyebrow">Security architecture</p>
  <h1>Know where profile data and access live.</h1>
  <p class="lead">AliasMode separates browser profiles, makes Local and Cloud explicit modes, and gives Cloud workspaces device, version, concurrency, and deletion controls.</p>

  <div class="grid security-grid">
    <section class="card"><h2>Profile isolation</h2><p>Each profile has a persistent user-data directory with its own cookies, session state, extensions, proxy, user agent, screen values, and fingerprint seed.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>Local boundary</h2><p>Local mode requires no AliasMode account, sends no traffic to AliasMode Cloud, and keeps AliasMode profile data on that computer.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>Cloud access</h2><p>Cloud uses a verified email and password. Each account has one workspace with owner and member roles, and workspace devices can be revoked.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>Synchronization controls</h2><p>Cloud synchronizes encrypted portable profiles, keeps a local cache, rejects stale uploads, retries pending uploads, and warns about concurrent opens.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>Deletion workflow</h2><p>Cloud workspaces include trash for deleted profiles. Keep profile lifecycle and client offboarding steps clear for every operator.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2>Release integrity</h2><p>The Windows beta publishes its release source and SHA-256 when an installer is available. The current beta is unsigned, so Windows can show SmartScreen.</p></section>
  </div>

  <section class="architecture-note">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Inspect the desktop client</p><h2>Apache-2.0 source is public.</h2></div>
    <div><p>The AliasMode desktop client is open source. CloakBrowser installs separately under its own license, and AliasMode Cloud is a managed service.</p><a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/aliasmode/aliasmode">View the desktop source</a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="report"><h2>Report a security issue</h2>{siteConfig.securityEmail ? <p>Send a responsible report to <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.securityEmail}`}>{siteConfig.securityEmail}</a>. Include the affected component, version, reproduction steps, and expected impact.</p> : <p>Security contact details will be published with the production site.</p>}</section>
  <RelatedLinks paths={['/product/', '/local/', '/cloud/']} title="Review each product boundary" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .security-grid { gap: .8rem; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); margin-top: 3rem; }
  .security-grid p { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: .9rem; }
  .architecture-note { align-items: start; background: linear-gradient(150deg, var(--night), #241d47); border-radius: var(--r-lg); color: #fff; display: grid; gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; margin-top: 4rem; padding: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .architecture-note .eyebrow { color: #b7a1ff; }
  .architecture-note h2 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.6vw, 2.8rem); }
  .architecture-note p:not(.eyebrow) { color: var(--night-ink); }
  .report { border-left: .35rem solid var(--violet); margin-top: 4rem; padding: 1rem 0 1rem 1.5rem; }
  @media (max-width: 54rem) { .security-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }.architecture-note { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  @media (max-width: 36rem) { .security-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
